==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Prof. Wild Base (Enemy Base)|Prof. Wild Base]].
*1 [[Hater]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 75% HP:
**5 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
**3 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
**3 [[Hater]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**1 [[Rain D.]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 50% HP:
**8 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
**3 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**6 [[Hater]]s spawn, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
**2 [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] spawn, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Social distancing from the base allows for avoiding the [[Slow]] and [[Weaken]], as well as to prevent setting off the 75% and 50% enemy waves. However, science denial should be used against this professor as there is no [[Boss Shockwave]] and the base is vulnerable to [[Surge Attacks]] and [[Explosion]]s, allowing it to be killed rapidly if multiple of those types of units hit it at once, such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] supported by any Surger. If it is not killed by the first combo, simply pin the enemies with meatshields or a tank like [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Curling Cat]] and finish it off with LD units.

